Chief Operating Officer (COO)
Position Overview

The Chief Operating Officer (COO) is responsible for the company's overall operational strategy, operational systems, business management, and strategic execution. The role encompasses the development of operational systems, organizational management, business process optimization, cross-departmental collaboration, operational efficiency enhancement, business growth, and international business operations.

The COO ensures that all operational functions operate efficiently, stably, and in a standardized manner. They continuously optimize organizational structures and business processes, improve resource allocation, operational quality, and execution capabilities, and drive the effective implementation of the company's overall strategy within its global jewelry business.

Key Responsibilities
1. Corporate Operational Strategy and Business Management

Formulate and implement the company's medium- to long-term operational strategies and business development plans;
Establish and continuously optimize the company-wide operational management system;
Translate strategic goals into concrete operational plans, management mechanisms, and execution initiatives;
Optimize organizational structure, business processes, and operational management models;
Establish company-wide operational standards, management policies, and working mechanisms;
Coordinate daily operations across business departments, ensuring that operational functions operate in a standardized, efficient, and collaborative manner.

2. Business Operations and Organizational Collaboration

Oversee the operational management of core business areas and functional departments;
Establish efficient cross-departmental collaboration mechanisms to enhance overall organizational execution efficiency;
Analyze operational status, market changes, customer needs, and business performance data;
Identify key operational issues, business opportunities, and areas for efficiency improvement;
Drive the effective implementation of key business initiatives, strategic projects, and major operational plans;
Coordinate resources across departments to ensure alignment between overall business goals and operational plans.

3. Operational Systems and Process Management

Establish and refine the company's operational management policies, processes, and standards;
Continuously optimize business processes, approval workflows, management procedures, and cross-departmental collaboration workflows;
Drive the standardization, regulation, and digitalization of operational processes;
Establish mechanisms for operational performance management and business monitoring;
Optimize resource allocation, staffing, and business execution models;
Enhance overall operational efficiency, execution quality, and organizational responsiveness. 4. Operational Performance and Resource Management

Establish overall corporate operational goals, performance indicators, and management systems;
Formulate annual, quarterly, and monthly operational objectives and execution plans;
Analyze business and operational data as well as Key Performance Indicators (KPIs);
Monitor the operational performance and goal achievement of various business units;
Optimize the allocation of resources, including personnel, capital, supply chain, production, sales, and other operational assets;
Identify opportunities to improve operational costs, efficiency, and profitability;
Drive continuous improvement in overall operational efficiency, business performance, and profitability.

5. Cross-functional Collaboration and Business Support

Collaborate with sales, marketing, product, procurement, supply chain, production, customer service, finance, and other departments;
Establish efficient cross-functional operational collaboration processes;
Ensure departmental operational goals align with the company's overall business strategy;
Coordinate product, supply chain, production, and customer service capabilities based on market and customer demands;
Drive the successful implementation of key client business, strategic projects, and major operational initiatives;
Provide operational management support for new market entry, product launches, and international business expansion;
Coordinate the resolution of major cross-departmental business issues to ensure the stable operation of core business activities.

6. Risk, Compliance, and Operational Management

Identify potential risks within company operations, business processes, supply chains, and commercial partnerships;
Establish mechanisms for operational risk monitoring, early warning, and emergency management;
Ensure operational activities comply with relevant laws, regulations, and industry standards;
Strengthen internal controls, process management, and operational oversight;
Standardize procedures for business execution, contract management, and cross-departmental collaboration;
Establish management and emergency response mechanisms for major operational matters;
Ensure stable, sustainable, and compliant business growth. Qualifications

15–20 years of experience in operations management, corporate management, business management, or related fields;
At least 5 years of experience in senior management roles at the Director level or above;
Experience in overall operations management within large enterprises or multinational corporations;
Experience in the jewelry, luxury goods, retail, or manufacturing sectors is preferred;
Experience in international business, global operations, or cross-border business management is preferred;
Extensive experience in cross-departmental management, business operations, and strategic project management;
Proven capabilities in operational strategic planning, organizational management, process optimization, and execution;
Exceptional skills in data analysis, business acumen, operational management, and decision-making;
Outstanding leadership, communication, coordination, and cross-functional collaboration skills.

We Offer

Competitive compensation and benefits packages;
Long-term career development and advancement opportunities;
The opportunity to join the core executive team of a rapidly growing enterprise.

